From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pb01ka <gaganpb08singh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bump vendored Highway 1.3.0 -> 1.4.0 for clang 22 evex512
 compat

TF 2.21.0 pins com_google_highway at 1.3.0. Highway 1.3.0's
hwy/ops/x86_512-inl.h does not account for clang's AVX10-driven
evex512 target-feature split, so any TU that includes it fails to
build under clang >= 22 with e.g.:

  error: always_inline function '_mm512_div_ps' requires target
  feature 'avx512f', but would be inlined into function 'operator/'
  that is compiled without support for 'avx512f'
  error: AVX vector return of type '__m512' (vector of 16 'float'
  values) without 'avx512f' enabled changes the ABI

This is a known, already-fixed upstream issue (google/highway#1864):
confirmed broken on 1.3.0, confirmed fixed on 1.4.0, with no source
change needed on our side beyond re-pointing the pin. sha256 verified
against the GitHub release tarball for tag 1.4.0.

TF's own third_party/com_google_highway/build.patch (applied on top of
whichever Highway tarball is fetched, to move highway.h/foreach_target.h
from textual_hdrs into hdrs with an include_prefix) is line-number-exact
against 1.3.0's BUILD file and does not apply against 1.4.0's, whose BUILD
file shifted around it. Ported it to the same hunks against 1.4.0's
actual BUILD content (same transformation, verified by hand against the
1.4.0 release tarball); no functional change from the original intent.
---
--- a/third_party/com_google_highway/workspace.bzl
+++ b/third_party/com_google_highway/workspace.bzl
@@ -5,8 +5,8 @@ load("//third_party:repo.bzl", "tf_http_archive", "tf_mirror_urls")
 def repo():
     tf_http_archive(
         name = "com_google_highway",
-        strip_prefix = "highway-1.3.0",
-        sha256 = "07b3c1ba2c1096878a85a31a5b9b3757427af963b1141ca904db2f9f4afe0bc2",
-        urls = tf_mirror_urls("https://github.com/google/highway/archive/refs/tags/1.3.0.tar.gz"),
+        strip_prefix = "highway-1.4.0",
+        sha256 = "e72241ac9524bb653ae52ced768b508045d4438726a303f10181a38f764a453c",
+        urls = tf_mirror_urls("https://github.com/google/highway/archive/refs/tags/1.4.0.tar.gz"),
         patch_file = ["//third_party/com_google_highway:build.patch"],
     )
--- a/third_party/com_google_highway/build.patch
+++ b/third_party/com_google_highway/build.patch
@@ -1,13 +1,22 @@
-diff --git a/BUILD b/BUILD
-index ef49b2d..1710abc 100644
---- a/BUILD
-+++ b/BUILD
-@@ -157,1 +155,5 @@ cc_library(
-+        "hwy/highway.h",  # public
-+        "hwy/foreach_target.h",  # public
-     ],
-+    include_prefix = "third_party/highway",
-+    includes = ["."],
-@@ -169,2 +173,0 @@ cc_library(
--        "hwy/highway.h",  # public
--        "hwy/foreach_target.h",  # public
+diff --git a/BUILD b/BUILD
+--- a/BUILD
++++ b/BUILD
+@@ -155,7 +155,11 @@
+         "hwy/detect_compiler_arch.h",  # private
+         "hwy/print.h",
+         "hwy/x86_cpuid.h",
++        "hwy/highway.h",  # public
++        "hwy/foreach_target.h",  # public
+     ],
++    include_prefix = "third_party/highway",
++    includes = ["."],
+     compatible_with = [],
+     copts = COPTS,
+     defines = DEFINES,
+@@ -168,6 +172,4 @@
+         "hwy/per_target.cc",
+         # End of list
+-        "hwy/highway.h",  # public
+-        "hwy/foreach_target.h",  # public
+         "hwy/per_target.h",  # public
+         "hwy/print-inl.h",  # public
